# Material You

Use Google Material Design 3 for every UI change. Do not invent a parallel visual language.

- Tokens only: `var(--md-sys-color-*)`, `var(--md-sys-typescale-*)`, `var(--md-sys-shape-*)`. No one-off hex in components.
- Type: Roboto. Icons: Material Symbols Outlined.
- Shapes: 8 / 12 / 16 / 28px. Buttons 40dp. FAB 56dp. Text fields outlined.
- Use MD3 patterns: navigation drawer, assist chips, tonal/filled/text buttons, FAB, side/bottom sheets, dialogs, cards.
- Color comes from the Pittsburgh gold seed in `src/theme/material.css`. Do not revert to default MUI purple or the old custom gold/black theme.
- Interactive states use on-surface opacity (8% hover, 12% focus), not new border colors.
- Prefer existing components (`StarRating`, `ReviewForm`, sheets) over new one-off widgets.

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
.card { background: #1a1714; border-radius: 5px; font-family: Outfit; }

/* ✅ GOOD */
.card {
  background: var(--md-sys-color-surface-container);
  border-radius: var(--md-sys-shape-large);
}
```
